            <ArticleTitle>[Comparative changes of TNF-alpha levels in occupational bronchial asthma patients under exposure to phytotherapy complexes and conventional corticosteroid therapy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>24-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Occupational bronchial asthma patients appeared to have various serum levels of Tumor Necrosis Factor alpha before initiation of phytotherapy complexes treatment. After taking phytotherapy complexes the levels of TNF-alpha normalized. That caused lower incidence of occupational bronchial asthma exacerbations and longer remission periods.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
